ving descended from his Puşpaka car he with silent approached Vāli to bring him under his grasp.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.885,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-34-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7034012","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3ed8e147db224bec3bf237eb9fb8dce98c2f65a53eebd69700588d067b6b1e4a","compact":"d86cfa78d07e54e89af018dda6afe7c18b852fe2e221baebdac454f461029911","nasal":"aa1b44b8c58c841aa40b254a9482a7158783a97b3f954b522839d24c6be4b0bd"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-34-13","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":34,"verse":13,"english":"Casting his looks at pleasure, Vali saw him. Albeit apprised of his evil intention, he was not the least moved. And he did not care for him as a lion is not moved on beholding a hare and Garuda on beholding a serpent.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.322,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-34-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7034013","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e26d0ef32157848416fece4865c08b58da6b2f7f27b612634a64ede9b4afbfa2","compact":"dfe77046eac1d0f825a0a7afebdcca7f5199ffff408741ade6b436187f20e7f0","nasal":"5d6aaed3321b1c8a59d5ce598e5a0689f621d4db42f23a0f59e8135251d9e25b"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-34-14","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":34,"verse":14,"english":"Casting his looks at pleasure, Vali saw him. Albeit apprised of his evil intention, he was not the least moved. And he did not care for him as a lion is not moved on beholding a hare and Garuda on beholding a serpent.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-34-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7034014","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c9f1a524788617a4d2b36b3ab1c10a31045fc5baf3967af5659