ga":34,"verse":29,"english":"And having journeyed over many thousand leagues like the wind and mind, that huge monkey, with his enemy, finished his prayers at the northern ocean and then proceeded to the eastern ocean.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.767,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-34-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7034029","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3987e706b6145c99a2100fcfcbd1ec23e2987093cd42b2ab10144cd9f6dab214","compact":"8c070b4df8368c77c693e9ed297840bcb07d9cd10e4e7f40fef1e1a925c6485c","nasal":"94e60ec8bfba18c71f8e266e1219f6bf89f9a8db54aab0a11349d97611e83554"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-34-30","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":34,"verse":30,"english":"And having recited his prayers there also, Vali, the son of Indra, and the king of monkeys, carrying Rāvana, returned to the city of Kişikindhā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.812,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-34-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7034030","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"de265e5b051b893990bf72121cca2a58408a3ef183ff8c34beab69e251b4f8ff","compact":"0d23b89cdbe50ccd69ad98ebbbd74137ac361c641d13cbab5497156f055505c7","nasal":"7436b44630e651b88256b95e4fdb820df17a629369960e256aefcee60fc7c82d"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-34-31","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":34,"verse":31,"english":"Having gone through his Sandhyā rites at the four oceans and carrying Răvaņa, that monkeychief was greatly exhausted and (therefore) descended into the gardens of Kişkindhā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.91,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-34-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7034031","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1e4158b99ca5438a64231e6ddffc715116f05bcd03ebcb3dbe198